// Title: Potential Persistence Via Logon Scripts - CommandLine
// Sigma ID: 21d856f9-9281-4ded-9377-51a1a6e2a432
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Tom Ueltschi (@c_APT_ure)
// Date: 2019-01-12 | Modified: 2023-06-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1037.001
// Description: Detects the addition of a new LogonScript to the registry value "UserInitMprLogonScript" for
//   potential persistence
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate addition of Logon Scripts via the command line by administrators or third party tools
// References:
//   - https://cocomelonc.github.io/persistence/2022/12/09/malware-pers-20.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_registry_logon_script.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "UserInitMprLogonScript"
